  "observations": "Personally inspected all three current13-model palace assembly views. North-up preserves the open central courtyard and distinct western/southern halls, eastern courtyard range and four additional irregular eastern roof bodies; there is no obvious major overlap from the new bodies. Obliques show the separate ranges stepping across the original hillside. Coarse source relief hides some uphill lower walls/roof portions and exposes other plinths; engineered historic benches and exact grade ties remain approximate. New eastern palace membership, exact royal/GoleGhar name, physical survival/date, height/storeys and facade/roof/finish are openly estimated. Original member dates2012/2023/2026are retained in an illustrative composite, not a certified same-date restored palace plan. All new appearance imagery unused. No existing9member geometry, field, frame, floor, section or QA changed.",
  "coverage": {
    "independentMembers": 13,
    "placedInstances": 13,
    "remainingLocalNativeFeatures": [],
    "scope": "Complete bounded palace-range reconstruction: nine independently completed courtyard/outer halls and post office plus four new original eastern roof bodies. All31/25/14/16new source corners retained; complex-wide written masonry/arch/joinery/cornice facts guide original estimated facades. Eastern palace membership, exact royal residence/GoleGhar assignment, survival/date, height/storeys/roof/finish are explicitly unverified estimates. This is a characteristic structure visualization, not a restored historic plan or survey of every royal room/ruin. Original dates and individual placements remain; ensemble2026is illustrative, not a certified simultaneous state. All new appearance imagery unused and all existing9member geometry/QA unchanged."
